  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 drops any numeric permanent failure limit and any sales stop, so a model above 5% (Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%) can keep selling while it files a corrective-action plan; per-model results go to owners and buyers but not the public. S3 sets a 72-month retrofit for 90% of compatible installed units, which matches Northwind's 6-year red line, and S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which would capture Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) but not Northwind's flagship (6.4). S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, which is stricter than either company's current practice given their unreported incidents."
